textual approximation of nothing while still technically responding is \"...\" or perhaps a blank line.\n\nI'll go with \"...\" — it is universally recognized as silence in text. Or should I dare to send nothing? The system says output only what the concept would express. Silence expresses through absence. \"...\" IS the symbol of that absence in language.\n\nFinal answer: \"...\""},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":442,"total_tokens":565,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":426},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}